<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">al-Mu'ayyad Muhammad</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1582">1582</a>–<a href="/years/1644">1644</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Also known as al-Mu'ayyad Muhammad ibn al-Qasim</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Al-Mu'ayyad Muhammad was the Zaydi <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/imam">imam</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yemen">Yemen</a> from 1620 to 1644 and the second ruler of the Qasimid State. Continuing the revolt begun by his father al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, he drove the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a> from the highlands, took Sanaa and forced them to evacuate Yemen in 1636. His success made the Qasimid family masters of the whole country.</p></div>
